{
  "requirement": "`LanguageId` is a public struct with a private string. Construct one from `&str`\nor `String`, for example `LanguageId::from(\"rust\")`. `as_str()` borrows the\noriginal name. Serde represents the identifier as a string.\n\n`StructuralQuery::language` takes a `LanguageId`. Construction preserves the\nspelling. Structural search looks up the name among the configured languages\nand returns an error for an unknown name.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct LanguageId(/* private fields */);\n\nimpl LanguageId {\n    pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for LanguageId;\nimpl Debug for LanguageId;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for LanguageId;\nimpl From<&str> for LanguageId;\nimpl From<String> for LanguageId;\nimpl Hash for LanguageId;\nimpl PartialEq for LanguageId;\nimpl Serialize for LanguageId;\nimpl Eq for LanguageId;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.language_id`.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n- **Construction from `&str` and `String`.** `source_bytes_error_kinds_and_language_names_round_trip` builds `LanguageId::from(\"CustomLang\")` and `LanguageId::from(String::from(\"CustomLang\"))`. It asserts the two are equal, which also exercises `PartialEq` and `Eq`.\n- **`as_str()` borrows the original name, and construction preserves the spelling.** The same test asserts `as_str() == \"CustomLang\"`. The mixed-case spelling would expose any normalization.\n- **Serde represents the identifier as a string.** The test asserts `serde_json::to_value` gives the JSON string `\"CustomLang\"`. It then deserializes that value and compares it with the original.\n- **`StructuralQuery::language` takes a `LanguageId`.** Both marked tests call `StructuralQuery::new(LanguageId, ..)`. `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` also reads `query.language` and clones it, which exercises `Clone`.\n- **Structural search looks up the name among the configured languages.** The project-scope test searches with `\"rust\".into()` and `\"python\".into()`. It asserts the correct files match, and that the Python search finds only `script.py`. The lookup therefore resolves known names to the right language.\n- **Structural search errors for an unknown name.** The round-trip test searches with `CustomLang` and asserts `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))`. The message must contain \"CustomLang\".\n- **Trait implementations listed in the requirement.** `Clone`, `Debug`, `Hash`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize` are all `#[derive]`s on the struct in `src/sources/public.rs`. Only `Clone`, `PartialEq`/`Eq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize` are exercised. `Debug` and `Hash` are not tested directly. They are plain derives with no conditional or transformation of their own, so I treated that as covered by the exemption for pass-through code. `public_exports_match_the_appendix`, which carries a `requirements.sdk.public_api` reference, checks that the public inventory compiles and matches.\n- **Public struct with a private string.** The tuple field is private, and the tests can only construct the type through `From`.\n\nI found no uncovered obligation and no assertion that contradicts the text. No {fixme} acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "3c2a02796d0ce8a489570e43492c83c3123514508b0835799933c75335ff0a73",
